Question: Explain to me how to ride a bike like I am a kid. Also, do not include the keywords "slow", "like" and "kid".

[HARD CONSTRAINT] You must also AVOID using the following common words: 'that'.
Init_answer: Riding a bike is super fun. First, you need to wear a helmet to keep your head safe. Make sure it fits properly.

Next, find a flat place to ride, like a park or empty parking lot. Look for smooth ground without any rocks or sticks.

Now, get on the bike and sit on the seat. Hold onto the handlebars and make sure your feet are on the pedals. You should be able to put one foot on a pedal and push off with the other.

Push one pedal down with one foot to make the bike move. Keep pushing the pedals round and round to keep going. Remember to keep your balance by leaning a little bit to one side.

When you want to stop, squeeze the brakes with your hands. This will make the bike stop moving.

If you fall off, don't worry. Just get back on the bike and try again. Practice makes perfect, so keep trying until you feel comfortable riding a bike.
