Init_answer: Imagine you're a farmer who grows yummy fruits. You work hard to grow them, but you can't eat them all by yourself. You want to trade them for things you need, like food for your family or a new bike.

When you trade your fruits for something you want, you're using something called time. You spent time growing those fruits, so now you can use them to get something else. This is like trading time for money.

